Condition : 21 - No development shall take place until a detailed Demolition, Construction and Environmental Management Plan (CEMP) has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CEMP shall be accompanied by details of how demolition and construction work for that phase are to be undertaken and include:
a)	The identification of stages of works;
b)	Details of working hours, which unless otherwise agreed with the Local Planning Authority shall be limited to 08.00 to 18.00 Monday to Friday and 08.00 to 13.00 on Saturdays);
c)	Procedures for maintaining good public relations including complaint management, public consultation and liaison;
d)	Mitigation measures as defined in BS 5228: Parts 1 and 2: 2009 Noise and Vibration Control on Construction and Open Sites shall be used to minimise noise disturbance construction works.

(a)	A Site Waste Management Strategy identifying all waste streams arising from the demolition and construction phases, including measures for waste minimisation, segregation, storage, recycling, recovery, transportation and disposal;

(b)	A comprehensive asbestos survey (including any Refurbishment and Demolition Asbestos Survey, where required) undertaken by a suitably qualified and competent person. The survey shall identify the presence, extent and condition of any asbestos-containing materials and shall include details of the measures necessary for their safe removal, handling, transportation and disposal in accordance with relevant legislation and guidance;

(c)	Copies of demolition and waste disposal contracts, or details of the appointed contractors and disposal facilities, demonstrating how demolition arisings, hazardous materials and asbestos-containing materials will be managed and lawfully disposed of at appropriately licensed facilities.

